      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stella%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1900, the Louisiana and San Francisco Railroad sold part of what became Stella to Moses Eagle for $200.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stella%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Lentz‑Carter Merchandise Store earned a spot on the National Register of Historic Places in 2008.",
